## Skill 9: Performance Optimization

### Code Splitting
```typescript
// Lazy load admin pages
const DashboardPage = React.lazy(() => import('./pages/admin/DashboardPage'))
const BlogEditor = React.lazy(() => import('./pages/admin/BlogEditor'))

// Wrap in Suspense
<Suspense fallback={<PageSkeleton />}>
  <Route path="/admin" element={<DashboardPage />} />
</Suspense>
```

### Optimization Rules
- Admin pages: ALWAYS lazy loaded (code split)
- Public pages: HomePage eager, rest lazy
- Components > 50KB: consider lazy loading
- Use `React.memo()` for pure display components in lists
- Use `useMemo` / `useCallback` only when measured performance issue
- Avoid re-renders: lift state up, use context sparingly

